<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via $1.5 bln customer RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via $1.5 bln customer RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system via a round of $1.5 billion in customer repurchase agreements Monday, the Federal Reserve Bank of New York confirmed.</p>
<p>Economists surveyed by Reuters prior to the midday intervention had been expecting a round of multiple-day system RPs. Fed funds were trading at 5-1/4 percent at the time of the intervention.</p>
<p>--John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663</p>
</text>
